.B Start\-Claude.ps1
is the script for Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the conversation of a schedule in the clone you are in, starting it in
claude's background when it has none:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --schedule 916
.fi
.PP
On a schedule in another repository:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --schedule NobleFactor/devlore-cli#916
.fi
.PP
Open a workspace for another clone without leaving this one:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --directory ~/Workspace/NobleFactor/noblefactor-engprod --schedule NobleFactor/devlore-cli#916
.fi
.PP
Open it on another host, and come back to your own shell when you leave it:
.PP
.nf
\&ssh -t \fIhost\fP 'Start-Claude --directory \fIclone\fP --schedule 916'
.fi
.PP
From a script, with no terminal: start the conversation in claude's background
if none runs, and leave it for Remote Control:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --detach --directory \fIclone\fP --schedule 916
.fi
.PP
Open a conversation by its identifier, on its schedule when the store holds it:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --resume 2ee3ba2e-2687-412d-8a4f-eabc597824ac
.fi
.PP
Put a conversation started elsewhere on a schedule, and open it there:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --resume 2ee3ba2e-2687-412d-8a4f-eabc597824ac --schedule 916
.fi
.PP
Open a conversation by its name, or by its background session's short
identifier:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --resume 'release checklist'
\&Start-Claude --resume 2ee3ba2e
.fi
.PP
Open, in the clone you are in, the conversation claude lists there, or else a
copy of the one claude picks:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --continue
.fi
.PP
Open a new schedule, asked for its title, or with the title piped:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --schedule new
\&echo 'Release 0.2' | Start-Claude --schedule new
.fi
.PP
Stop a schedule's conversation; the next start opens it again:
.PP
.nf
\&claude stop "$(cat ~/.local/state/agent-schedule/NobleFactor/devlore-cli/916)"
.fi
.PP
Give the shell pane a third of the window:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --schedule 916 --shell-width-percent 33
.fi
.PP
Pass arguments through to a conversation the launch starts:
.PP
.nf
\&Start-Claude --schedule 916 -- --model opus
.fi
